1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,193
Ava: The PyTorch Foundation is celebrating the people whose work advances open source projects and strengthens the communities around them.
Ava：PyTorch Foundation 正在表彰那些推动开源项目发展、壮大周边社区的人们。

2
00:00:09,193 --> 00:00:16,334
The recognition took place on the keynote stage at PyTorch Conference 2026 in San Jose, California.
该表彰活动在加利福尼亚州圣何塞举行，地点是 PyTorch Conference 2026 的主题演讲舞台。

3
00:00:16,334 --> 00:00:21,702
Brian: It's the fourth annual PyTorch Foundation Contributor Awards.
Brian：这是第四届 PyTorch Foundation Contributor Awards（贡献者奖）。

4
00:00:21,702 --> 00:00:29,974
At a glance, 2026 has 15 award winners, 11 nominees, 9 award categories, and 3 new categories.
概览：2026 年共有 15 位获奖者、11 位提名者、9 个奖项类别和 3 个新增类别。

5
00:00:29,974 --> 00:00:43,084
The winner count is up from 11 in 2025, and the recognition spans PyTorch Foundation-hosted projects including PyTorch, vLLM, Ray, and DeepSpeed.
获奖者人数从 2025 年的 11 人增加到今年的 15 人，表彰范围涵盖 PyTorch Foundation 主办的项目，包括 PyTorch、vLLM、Ray 和 DeepSpeed。

6
00:00:43,084 --> 00:00:46,993
Ava: Those new categories make the program's scope clearer.
Ava：这些新增类别让项目的覆盖范围更加清晰。

7
00:00:46,993 --> 00:00:50,685
Contribution isn't limited to technical innovation.
贡献并不局限于技术创新。

8
00:00:50,685 --> 00:00:56,754
What does each category recognize, and how does it extend the older categories?
每个类别表彰什么，又如何扩展了原有类别？

9
00:00:56,754 --> 00:01:06,920
Brian: Knowledge Enhancer celebrates contributors who make knowledge more accessible through documentation, tutorials, and educational resources.
Brian：“Knowledge Enhancer（知识增进奖）”表彰通过文档、教程和教育资源让知识更易获取的贡献者。

10
00:01:06,920 --> 00:01:15,244
Bug Buster recognizes people who identify, report, and resolve bugs that improve project quality and reliability.
“Bug Buster（缺陷修复奖）”表彰发现、报告并解决漏洞，从而提升项目质量和可靠性的人士。

11
00:01:15,244 --> 00:01:24,157
Catalyst honors contributions that improve developer workflows, automation, infrastructure, and AI-supported development.
“Catalyst（催化剂奖）”表彰改善开发者工作流、自动化、基础设施和 AI 辅助开发的贡献。

12
00:01:24,157 --> 00:01:34,304
These additions complement existing categories for technical innovation, mentorship, community leadership, and ecosystem development.
这些新增类别补充了现有的技术创新、导师指导、社区领导力和生态系统发展类别。

13
00:01:34,304 --> 00:01:40,416
Ava: The winner list shows that range. In Superhero, Thomas Ortner won for PyTorch.
Ava：获奖名单体现了这种广度。在 “Superhero（超级英雄奖）”类别中，Thomas Ortner 因 PyTorch 获奖。

14
00:01:40,416 --> 00:01:44,021
Guangye Yu was the PyTorch Ecosystem Champion.
Guangye Yu 获得 PyTorch Ecosystem Champion（PyTorch 生态冠军奖）。

15
00:01:44,021 --> 00:01:51,387
The two Knowledge Enhancers were Abdulsalam Yazid Bande for PyTorch and Suman Debnath for Ray.
两位 Knowledge Enhancer 得主是：PyTorch 项目的 Abdulsalam Yazid Bande，以及 Ray 项目的 Suman Debnath。

16
00:01:51,387 --> 00:01:58,006
The Bug Busters were Guilherme Vieira Leobas and Vishal Goyal, both for PyTorch.
Bug Buster 得主是 Guilherme Vieira Leobas 和 Vishal Goyal，两人均来自 PyTorch 项目。

17
00:01:58,006 --> 00:02:05,222
Brian: Then come two Newcomers: Johannes Lennart Zeiser for PyTorch and Jiangyun Zhu for vLLM.
Brian：接下来是两位 Newcomer（新人奖）得主：PyTorch 项目的 Johannes Lennart Zeiser，以及 vLLM 项目的 Jiangyun Zhu。

18
00:02:05,222 --> 00:02:08,623
Wentao Ye won Review Powerhouse for vLLM.
Wentao Ye 凭借 vLLM 获得 Review Powerhouse（评审主力奖）。

19
00:02:08,623 --> 00:02:18,180
The Innovator category went to Elfie Guo for PyTorch, Masahiro Tanaka for DeepSpeed, and Xinan Lin for PyTorch.
Innovator（创新者奖）授予 PyTorch 项目的 Elfie Guo、DeepSpeed 项目的 Masahiro Tanaka，以及 PyTorch 项目的 Xinan Lin。

20
00:02:18,180 --> 00:02:23,016
Ava: The remaining awards were Catalyst and Outstanding Ambassador.
Ava：剩余奖项是 Catalyst 和 Outstanding Ambassador。

21
00:02:23,016 --> 00:02:33,156
Harry Mellor won Catalyst for vLLM, Jiahao Tan won Catalyst for PyTorch, and Jiho Kim received Outstanding Ambassador for PyTorch.
Harry Mellor 凭借 vLLM 获得 Catalyst，Jiahao Tan 凭借 PyTorch 获得 Catalyst，Jiho Kim 则凭借 PyTorch 获得 Outstanding Ambassador（杰出大使奖）。

22
00:02:33,156 --> 00:02:38,186
That accounts for all 15 winners across the nine categories.
这涵盖了九个类别中的全部 15 位获奖者。

23
00:02:38,186 --> 00:02:56,803
Brian: The program also recognizes 11 nominees: Chandra Mohan Singh Negi, Arun Bhandari, Masahiro Hiramori, Luka Govedič, Irakli Salia, Jiahao Chen, Kunshang Ji, Rohit Kumar Tiwari, Subin George, Aaron Gokaslan, and Xunzhuo Liu.
Brian：该项目还表彰 11 位提名者：Chandra Mohan Singh Negi、Arun Bhandari、Masahiro Hiramori、Luka Govedič、Irakli Salia、Jiahao Chen、Kunshang Ji、Rohit Kumar Tiwari、Subin George、Aaron Gokaslan 和 Xunzhuo Liu。

24
00:02:56,803 --> 00:03:03,808
Their contributions continue to make a difference across the PyTorch ecosystem.
他们的贡献持续为整个 PyTorch 生态系统带来积极影响。

25
00:03:03,808 --> 00:03:13,157
Ava: You can watch the award ceremony at PyTorch Conference North America and explore the 2026 Contributor Awards to view the honorees.
Ava：你可以在 PyTorch Conference North America 观看颁奖典礼，并查看 2026 Contributor Awards 了解获表彰者。

26
00:03:13,157 --> 00:03:24,006
There's a special thank you to the Contributor Awards Program Committee and to Red Hat, sponsor of the 2026 PyTorch Foundation Contributor Awards.
特别感谢 Contributor Awards Program Committee，以及 2026 PyTorch Foundation Contributor Awards 的赞助商 Red Hat。

27
00:03:24,006 --> 00:03:30,250
Brian: So the useful takeaway is simple: 2026 expands recognition in both scale and scope.
Brian：所以，最实用的结论很简单：2026 年的表彰在规模和范围上都扩大了。

28
00:03:30,250 --> 00:03:45,899
There are 15 winners, 3 new categories, and contributors recognized for technical innovation, knowledge sharing, bug fixing, workflow improvements, mentorship, community leadership, and ecosystem development.
共有 15 位获奖者和 3 个新增类别，贡献者因技术创新、知识分享、漏洞修复、工作流改进、导师指导、社区领导力和生态系统发展而受到表彰。

29
00:03:45,899 --> 00:03:56,180
The Foundation says their work makes the ecosystem stronger, more collaborative, and more accessible to developers around the world.
基金会表示，他们的工作让生态系统更强大、更具协作性，也让世界各地的开发者更易参与。

30
00:03:56,180 --> 00:04:02,290
Ava: It's a broad definition of contribution, and this year's list makes it visible.
Ava：这是对贡献的广义定义，而今年的名单让它清晰可见。

31
00:04:02,290 --> 00:04:03,741
Brian: That's our briefing.
Brian：以上就是本期简报。

32
00:04:03,741 --> 00:04:09,168
Congratulations to every winner and nominee, and thanks for listening.
祝贺每一位获奖者和提名者，也感谢您的收听。
